  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is a rhyme family?",
      "a": "It is a group of words that end with the same letters and sound, like cat, hat and mat. Only the first sound changes.",
      "asks": [
        "What is a word family?",
        "Tell me about the at family"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "How do rhyme families help me read?",
      "a": "Once you know the ending, you only need to change the first sound. One word you know helps you read lots of new words.",
      "asks": [
        "Why learn word families?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I read a new word in a family?",
      "a": "Cover the first letter and read the ending. Then add the first sound and blend them together.",
      "asks": [
        "Tell me about the ig family"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Do all rhyming words look the same?",
      "a": "Not always. Blue and shoe rhyme, but they end with different letters. Families with the same letters are the easiest place to start.",
      "asks": [
        "Do rhymes always end the same?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What games can I play with rhyme families?",
      "a": "Try a rhyme chain: say cat, then hat, mat and sat. A teacher or grown-up can make letter cards so you can swap the first letter.",
